      "evidence": "The page says framed 0-manififolds of S^n are classified by signed count without restricting n. For n=0, S^0 has two points with opposite standard orientation signs, so the full set and the empty set both have signed count 0. They are not framed cobordant: a rank-zero cobordism in S^0×I is a union of whole component intervals, so occupancy at the two ends agrees. The in-scope zero-manifold example supplies the missing n≥1 hypothesis.",
